------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Provenance
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The decoder and encoder are original implementations written from ITU-T
Recommendation H.262 (02/2000), identical to ISO/IEC 13818-2:2000, and, for
the ISO/IEC 11172-2 (MPEG-1) points H.262 summarises in its Annex D.9,
knowledge of that standard. They are not translations of, and do not derive
from, any other MPEG-2 or MPEG-1 decoder's or encoder's source. The
normative tables (the variable length codes of Annex B, the scans of
Figures 7-2 and 7-3, the default quantiser matrices, Table 7-6) are
reproduced from the Recommendation.

The decoder is verified against the video conformance bitstreams of ISO/IEC
13818-4:2004, which ISO publishes among its Publicly Available Standards,
used as data: they are downloaded at test time (tools/fetch-conformance.sh)
and not included. No other implementation was run to make or check test
data.

